Third-Party Notices
===================

Kept out of LICENSE so that GitHub and other licence scanners can detect the
MIT licence. A LICENSE file with anything appended after the MIT text is
reported as NOASSERTION, which reads as "unlicensed" to tooling.

GDPRLetterBuilder ships no third-party code: no libraries, no packages, no
content delivery network. Every script it runs is Stormberry AS's own and is
published in this repository. The one third-party item it ships is a typeface.

The letters are Stormberry AS's own wording. They quote short phrases from the
GDPR, from its Norwegian text and from the Norwegian Personal Data Act
(personopplysningsloven); statutes and official decisions are not protected by
copyright in Norway (åndsverkloven § 14). No template from a data protection
authority or another project is copied.

